.TH CFX 1 "August 2, 2026" "cfx" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
cfx \- small, auditable Codeforces workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.I problem
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B pick
.RI [ handle ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B submit
.RB [ \-\-manual ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B test
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfx
manages an ordinary C++20 Codeforces solution archive.
The usual workflow is:
.PP
.nf
cfx 71A
cfx submit
.fi
.PP
The first command fetches the statement metadata and samples through the
browser connector, creates the problem directory, and opens
.IR solution.cpp .
The second tests and checked-compiles the exact bundled source, submits it
through the signed-in browser, and waits for the Codeforces verdict.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I problem
Fetch a problem, create
.IR codeforces/contest/index/ ,
open
.IR solution.cpp ,
and remember it as the current problem.
Official contest mirrors are tried when the primary statement is unavailable.
.TP
.BI "pick [" handle "]"
Look up the handle's current rating and randomly suggest one unsolved problem
from the first available 100-point rung at least 100 points higher, excluding
problems already present in the archive. An explicit handle is remembered for
later picks. This command does not fetch the selected statement, create its
archive directory, or open an editor.
.TP
.BR test " [" problem "]"
Bundle and compile the solution, then run fetched samples followed by
handwritten cases.
Every input requires a matching expected-output file.
Report OK, WA, RE, TLE, MLE, or OLE with resource use.
.TP
.BR submit " [" problem "]"
Run every saved test, checked-compile the exact bundled source, submit it
through Chrome, and report the verdict and official resource use.
Only
.B OK
on
.B TESTS
is Accepted.
.B PRETESTS
and known pending submissions exit 2; a final non-Accepted verdict exits 1.
When the connector is unavailable, copy the tested source to the clipboard and
open the submission page.
No password or session cookie is read or stored.
.TP
.BR help " [" command "]"
Display general help or help for one command.
.SH TEST OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-checked
Compile with strict warnings, AddressSanitizer, and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
.TP
.BI "\-\-time-limit " seconds
Override the fetched time limit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-memory-limit " MiB
Override the fetched memory limit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-output-limit " MiB
Override the output limit, which defaults to 64 MiB.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-manual
Copy the tested source to the clipboard and open the submission page instead
of using the connector.
.TP
.BI "\-\-root " directory
Use
.I directory
as the archive root.
.SH PROBLEM IDENTIFIERS
Explicit problems use only the canonical Codeforces form, for example
.BR 71A .
When run beneath
.IR codeforces/contest/index/ ,
commands infer the problem.
.B submit
may also use the most recently opened problem.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/solution.cpp
User solution.
.TP
.I .cfx/solution.cpp
Optional archive-owned starter template.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/cases/
Handwritten cases.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/problem.json
Fetched problem metadata and resource limits.
.TP
.I include/cp/
Optional archive-owned competitive-programming headers or library submodule.
.TP
.I include/peek/
Optional archive-owned
.B peek
diagnostics submodule.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cfx/workspaces/
Fetched samples, the cached problem catalogue, builds, run output,
current-problem state, the remembered picker handle, and prepared submissions.
When
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset, cfx uses
.IR $HOME/.local/state/cfx/workspaces/ .
.SH LIBRARIES
.B cfx
ships no C++ support headers.
The separate, extensionless
.B cp
algorithm library and single-header
.B peek
diagnostics library can be added independently:
.PP
.nf
git submodule add https://github.com/njlane314/cp include/cp
git submodule add https://github.com/njlane314/peek include/peek
.fi
.PP
Include only the required components. For example:
.PP
.nf
#include <cp/fenwick_tree>
.fi
.PP
.B cfx
defines
.B PEEK_COMPILED=1
for local builds and
.B PEEK_COMPILED=0
for submission builds, so a solution only needs:
.PP
.nf
#include <peek.hpp>
.fi
.PP
When compiling outside
.BR cfx ,
apply the equivalent policy before the include:
.PP
.nf
#ifdef LOCAL
#define PEEK_COMPILED 1
#else
#define PEEK_COMPILED 0
#endif
#include <peek.hpp>
.fi
.PP
.B cfx
expands selected headers and their transitive includes into the exact source
compiled and submitted. Its default solution template remains dependency-free.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CXX
C++ compiler command; the default is
.BR c++ .
.TP
.B CFX_STD
C++ language standard; the default is
.BR c++20 .
.TP
.B CFX_CXXFLAGS
Additional compiler flags.
.TP
.B CFX_ROOT
Explicit archive root.
.TP
.B CFX_STATE_ROOT
Explicit runtime-state root.
.TP
.B CFX_SOLUTION_TEMPLATE
Starter-template path used when an archive has no
.IR .cfx/solution.cpp .
.TP
.B CFX_CHROME_EXTENSION_ID
Allowed Chrome connector identity.
Installed launchers set this from the packaged extension ID.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used for
.IR solution.cpp .
.TP
.B VISUAL
Editor fallback.
.TP
.B CFX_BROWSER
Browser-opening command override.
.TP
.B CFX_CLIPBOARD
Clipboard command override.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation succeeded; for
.BR submit ,
the verdict was
.B OK
on
.BR TESTS .
.TP
.B 1
Testing failed, or submit received a final non-Accepted verdict.
.TP
.B 2
Usage was invalid, an operation failed, or submission is pending or requires
manual completion.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch and solve a problem:
.PP
.nf
cfx pick your_handle
cfx 71A
cfx submit
.fi
.PP
Run sanitizer-backed tests:
.PP
.nf
cfx test --checked
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR c++ (1),
.BR git (1)
